## Canceling namespace creation
<img width="800" alt="Screen Shot 2022-06-02 at 2 39 42 AM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20599230/171602469-c130cdf3-4441-410a-a76d-a4d0d85df46e.png">

## How it works

This PR depends on the fact that every time we use the NameNsDescription component, it is in a slot within the CruResource component.

So I used ` this.$parent.$emit` in NameNsDescription to allow CruResource to listen for an event from within the slot:

```js
selectNamespace(e) {
      if (e.value === '') {  // The blank value in the dropdown is labeled "Create a New Namespace"
        this.createNamespace = true;
        this.$parent.$emit('createNamespace', true);
      } else {
        this.createNamespace = false;
        this.$parent.$emit('createNamespace', false);
      }
    }
```

This allows CruResource to try to create the namespace before saving the new resource:

```js
try {
          const newNamespace = await this.$store.dispatch('cluster/create', {
            type:     NAMESPACE,
            metadata: { name: this.resource.metadata.namespace }
          }, { root: true });
          newNamespace.applyDefaults();
          newNamespace.save();
        } catch (error) {
          throw new Error(`Could not create the new namespace. ${ error }`);
        }
```

It's nice to have CruResource do the namespace creation because it means this PR doesn't need to touch very many files. We have dozens of forms that have CruResource with a NameNsDescription within a slot. This means all those forms get the new functionality without needing any direct changes.


## What's unfinished

There is no form validation for the new namespace, but there is another issue tracking that here https://github.com/rancher/dashboard/issues/4861 and it can be done in a separate PR. Maybe after https://github.com/rancher/dashboard/pull/4999 is merged.

Also, I haven't tested this with Epinio namespaces. Because the Epinio development environment would need this change to be based on a different branch, I'll address any Epinio changes in a separate PR.

